│ the `__getattr__` method of the object being checked. This meant that file-like wrappers that delegated their   │
│ `read` method via `__getattr__` were not correctly identified as readable streams in `_encode_files`.           │
│                                                                                                                 │
│     I replaced the `isinstance(..., _SupportsRead)` checks with `hasattr(..., 'read')` in                       │
│ `src/requests/models.py`, which correctly triggers `__getattr__` and allows these wrappers to be detected.      │
│                                                                                                                 │
│     Summary of changes:                                                                                         │
│     - Modified `src/requests/models.py` to use `hasattr(data, "read")` instead of `isinstance(data,             │
│ _SupportsRead)` in three locations to support `__getattr__`-based file wrappers.                                │
